# TRANGPIO GPIO Control Driver
#
#
# Transsion TRANGPIO driver configuration
#

config TRAN_TRANGPIO
    tristate "Transsion TRANGPIO driver"
    depends on PINCTRL
    default n
    help
      This driver provides a character device interface for controlling
      GPIOs via pinctrl states. It allows userspace applications to
      control multiple GPIO pins through a simple read/write interface.
      
      The driver supports:
      - Reading current GPIO states
      - Setting individual or multiple GPIO states
      - Device tree configuration for GPIO mappings
      - Configurable timing parameters
      
      To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the
      module will be called trangpio.
      
      Debug logging can be controlled at runtime via the debug_enabled
      module parameter without requiring compile-time configuration.

      Say Y here if you want to use TRAN GPIO control functionality.
      Say M to build it as a module (trangpio.ko).

      If unsure, say N.
